From 6c5c4292c8622734e3cb64e9810edfe85a84c9cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:26:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Scale a server's queue cuts by what they do to the
 queue

Replaces the per-address verdict. Each connection compares how far the queue fell with how far a cut brought down what it has in flight, its caps and the rate they allow; pi's cuts and the cut at a long queue scale by that, and the caps follow the round trip by the rest.
